 "narration": "Look at your hand. It looks like one smooth piece, but it is not. All living organisms are made of cells, and a cell is the smallest unit of an organism that can carry out the processes of life. Humans, oak trees and mushrooms are multicellular, made of millions or billions of cells working together. Other organisms, such as Amoeba, Paramecium, yeast and bacteria, are unicellular: just one cell that carries out every life process by itself. Cells are measured in micrometres, and 1 mm = 1000 µm. A typical animal cell is about 10 to 30 µm across, and many bacteria are only 1 to 5 µm long. The human eye can see objects down to roughly 0.1 mm, which is 100 µm. So individual cells are usually invisible to the unaided eye. We need a microscope to see them.",
 "narration_sentences": [
  "Look at your hand. It looks like one smooth piece, but it is not.",
  "All living organisms are made of cells, and a cell is the smallest unit of an organism that can carry out the processes of life.",
  "Humans, oak trees and mushrooms are multicellular, made of millions or billions of cells working together.",
  "Other organisms, such as Amoeba, Paramecium, yeast and bacteria, are unicellular: just one cell that carries out every life process by itself.",
  "Cells are measured in micrometres, and 1 mm = 1000 µm.",
  "A typical animal cell is about 10 to 30 µm across, and many bacteria are only 1 to 5 µm long.",
  "The human eye can see objects down to roughly 0.1 mm, which is 100 µm.",
  "So individual cells are usually invisible to the unaided eye.",
  "We need a microscope to see them."
 ],
